# Client transport follow-up

- Document-socket multiplexing is intentionally deferred. The current room-scoped
  socket contract isolates schema close codes and unhealthy rooms. Revisit only with
  measured browser/socket pressure and a protocol that can reject one room without
  physically closing healthy rooms on the shared connection.
- Recovery after a server restart with the browser online still waits on backoff:
  no browser signal says the server is back, so the first connection to get through
  depends on the randomized delay (Hocuspocus `maxDelay` 30 s, thread
  `persistentDelayMs` 30 s; observed 0.8–22 s). Peer success then pulls the other
  connections within ~0.5 s. Lowering those caps trades reconnect load for latency;
  revisit with production deploy-restart data. Affected paths:
  `hocuspocus-document-transport.ts`, `ws-reconnect.ts`.
